WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.300
With a little planning.

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.490
Positioning buttonholes
for your knits isn't hard.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.540
The Knit It Now Button Hole Placement Tool

4
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:13.980
will walk you through all the decisions
you need to make step-by-step and generate

5
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:19.500
knitting instructions so you can knit
bands with perfectly spaced buttonholes.

6
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:24.940
Start by entering the gauge of the stitch
pattern you'll use for your band.

7
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.940
Next, add the details of your buttons.

8
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.220
How many holes?

9
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.900
How long is the band?

10
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.260
What size button hole do you need?

11
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:38.500
How much space do you want from the top
and the bottom edges of the band?

12
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.820
Armed with your answers,
the Tool will generate your knitting

13
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:46.160
instructions and you won't
have to do any math.

